From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chu Qinghao <6337103+qinghao1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] bridge: single-threaded headless build for static hosting

Static hosts (GitHub Pages) cannot send COOP/COEP, so SharedArrayBuffer
is unavailable and the pthread build aborts at startup. This makes the
wasm -pthread flags conditional on VPX_WASM_PTHREADS (default ON, so the
local threaded build is unchanged) and marks the headless target with
VPX_WASM_SINGLE_THREADED when threads are off. Each thread creation on
the headless load path takes its designed fallback there instead of
aborting in std::thread's constructor: the script hang watchdog runs
unguarded, the texture and quadtree pools run inline, and the B2S overlay
file writer stays idle (its queue keeps the synchronous default save).
Everything else headless already runs on the game thread (the Noop
renderer runs synchronously, gameplay uses the sync HitQuadtree).

Target: vpinball/vpinball@64a480a96d1b972711fbb8eea014654c779b1e23

